<h2 class="g-h2" id="usage">Usage</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p>A pill gets its tooltip from <code>severityBadge</code>'s <code>definition</code>. Anything else: class <code>tooltip-target</code>, <code>tabindex="0"</code> so it can take focus, and the text in <code>data-tooltip</code>. The script finds both on load and on hover.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="behaviour">Behaviour</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The tip opens on pointer hover (not touch) and on focus, closes on Escape, blur, a press elsewhere or the anchor scrolling out of view, and follows the anchor on scroll and resize. Where the browser has the Popover API the tip is a manual popover, so no <code>overflow: hidden</code> container clips it; otherwise it moves to <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> while open.</p></div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The anchor's <code>aria-describedby</code> names the tip (<code>role="tooltip"</code>), so the definition is read after the label. Keep a tooltip to a definition: nothing the reader must act on.</p></div>

